1-# Resources
2-
3-Resources are owned by the board element they are attached to. Use explicit
4-CRUD operations against that element ID. Local payloads are grouped under
5:`.task-board/.resources/<elementID>/`; remote board-server uses the equivalent
6-element-scoped filesystem or MinIO object-key prefix.
7-
8-## Resource Types
9-
--
14-
15-## Commands
16-
17-```bash
18:# Create a resource
19:task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=TASK-260218-abc_design.md, type=precondition, content="...", description="Architecture design")'
20:task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=reports/TASK-260218-abc_results.md, type=outcome, content="...", description="Research findings")'
21-
22:# Replace an existing resource
23:task-board m 'update_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=reports/TASK-260218-abc_results.md, type=outcome, content="revised findings", description="Research findings v2")'
24:task-board resource update TASK-260218-abc ./TASK-260218-abc_results.md --name reports/TASK-260218-abc_results.md --type outcome
25-
26-# Adopt an existing orphaned local payload without rewriting it
27:task-board resource adopt TASK-260218-abc revisions/2/TASK-260218-abc_results.md --type outcome --description "Recovered result"
28-
29:# Delete a resource (destructive — requires --confirm)
30:task-board m --confirm 'delete_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=artifacts/obsolete/TASK-260218-abc_design.md)'
31:task-board resource delete TASK-260218-abc artifacts/obsolete/TASK-260218-abc_design.md --confirm
32-
33:# View resources on an element
34-task-board q --format compact 'get(TASK-260218-abc) { preconditionResources outcomeResources }'
35-```
36-
37-## Element-Owned Storage
38-
39-Resources from different tasks are not stored in one shared file pile. Each
40:element gets its own directory, and every resource attached to that element is
41-stored below it:
42-
43-```
44:.task-board/.resources/
45-├── TASK-260203-g7h8i9/
46-│   ├── findings/
47-│   │   └── investigation.md
48-│   ├── artifacts/
--
56-└── STORY-260203-d4e5f6/
57-    └── research.md         # outcome
58-```
59-
60:The resource `name` is a safe forward-slash-relative path. Agents may choose
61-the hierarchy that fits the artifact and nest it further as needed. Every
62-segment must be non-empty printable UTF-8 and must not be `.`, `..`, an
63-absolute/drive-qualified path, or contain a backslash. Raw forward slashes are
64-the only hierarchy delimiter; malformed URL escapes and encoded or repeatedly
65-encoded separators/traversal are rejected. Attach related files to the same
66:owning element; do not invent a generic board-wide resource task or write
67:payloads into `.task-board/.resources/` manually.
68-
69-Directories are structural nodes, not payloads. Resource CRUD, validation, and
70-handoff evidence recognize regular files only; a directory named like a report
71-cannot be adopted or used to satisfy outcome evidence.
72-
73-Local and board-server filesystem element deletion is journaled and
74:crash-recoverable. Direct resource CRUD first resolves any pending staged
75-element delete under the board mutation lock. MinIO element/subtree deletion
76-currently fails before mutation with the typed
77:`ErrAtomicResourceDeleteUnsupported` capability error; ordinary resource CRUD
78-remains available.
79-
80-References are tracked in `progress.md` as markdown links:
81-```markdown
82-## Precondition Resources
83:- [specs/auth/design.md](board-resource://TASK-260203-g7h8i9/precondition/specs/auth/design.md) — Architecture design
84-
85-## Outcome Resources
86:- [reports/TASK-260203-g7h8i9_results.md](board-resource://TASK-260203-g7h8i9/outcome/reports/TASK-260203-g7h8i9_results.md) — Research findings
87-```
88-
89-## Spawn Integration
90-
91:Precondition resources are automatically injected into agent prompts by `task-board spawn`. Full prompts preserve normal text inlining. Lite prompts use the resolved `agent_context.prompt.preconditions` policy: by default, text below `inline_bytes` is rendered inline, while larger text and binary resources are written read-only under `.temp/resources/` and represented by their name, description, byte count, SHA-256 digest, and local path. This means:
92-
93:1. Attach instructions/specs as precondition resources to a task
94-2. Run `task-board spawn TASK-XX --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max` — agent gets everything automatically
95:3. Agent saves results via `task-board m 'add_resource(..., type=outcome)'` on first write, then `update_resource(...)` for revisions
96-
97-## Best Practices
98-
99-- **Use preconditions for agent instructions** — attach design docs, specs, or step-by-step instructions before spawning
100-- **Use outcomes for work products** — research findings, analysis, implementation notes
101-- **Attach to the owning element** — pass the Task, Bug, Story, or Epic ID that owns the artifact; the storage layer groups its payloads under that element directory automatically
102:- **Use explicit create/update/delete** — `add_resource` / `resource add` must not silently overwrite; use `update_resource` / `resource update` when replacing an existing payload
103:- **Use adopt only for local repair** — `resource adopt` registers bytes already stored at `.resources/<elementID>/<relative-resource-path>` without rewriting them; a missing payload returns resource-not-found and an existing declaration returns resource-exists
104-- **Choose a useful hierarchy inside the owning element** — `findings/`, `artifacts/`, `reports/`, and `revisions/` are conventions, not a fixed schema; nest further when it makes the handoff easier to navigate
105:- **Use safe relative resource paths** — `/` separates validated path segments; empty, dot/traversal, absolute/drive-qualified, backslash, control-character, malformed escape, and encoded/repeatedly encoded separator or traversal forms are rejected in local and remote storage
106:- **Attach files, not folders** — directories only organize resource files and never satisfy resource existence or handoff evidence
107:- **Always use board commands** — never create/edit resource files or progress.md resource sections manually
108:- **Name handoff evidence with task scope** — keep the task ID in the resource path, for example `reports/TASK-260218-abc_architecture-design.md`, so `task-board handoff` can recognize it
109-- **Add descriptions** — the `description=` param adds a one-line description shown in spawn prompts
110-
