- CORRECTION to the rev1 entry's F2 (appended, history preserved): "the mutation-context/status/bootstrap surfaces needed one (landed plain refusals)" is wrong for the two body surfaces — the landed `ParseMutationContext`/`ParseStatusBody` refuse a forbidden identity with the SAME pinned `terminal_backend_protocol_error`; the pre-scans add only the Go error type (`*terminalbackend.Error`), and no wrapper exists for the bootstrap surface at all (landed `Store.Bind` refuses plain and uncoded). The wrappers stay as a documented redundancy with corrected notes.
- F1: a major-1 selection over an already-validated semver needs no integer parse — the major is the digit run before the first dot, so prefix `1.` is exact with no saturation class for huge foreign majors; the 14-version agreement battery against `CheckVersionTuple` (grammar faults, majors 0/2/3/10, a 2^64-scale major, prerelease/build spellings) proves no second model.
- F2: `bindingIdentity`'s old "no number can reach the digest by check ordering" comment was false exactly where extension values are untyped — the pre-transform walk must be structural (decode + walk), not an ordering claim; the direct-identity hostile battery (numbers, nested dups, trailing data, depth/size caps) pins the walk independently of the member arms that now fire first.
- AC: 65 of 66 rows driven through production entries by named tests (row 57 restated as a bound — no v1-v3-only reader exists on trunk; rows 61–66 are the rework rows; matrix in `internal/termbind/TRACEABILITY.md`). MUTATION EVIDENCE: 34 narrowing mutants plus one supplementary arm-delete row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 36/36 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical. Registry: 5.2 gap reworded to the row-57 bound, eight test citations added across four cases with mirror updates, digest re-derived `b09b5b9f…` (canonical bytes 167094), tracecheck green `63/574` with identical section ratios. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.

### TASK-260830-2056mm rev2 — Race-gate rework: per-subtest evidence universes
- REWORKED after the rev1 CR validation stopped at command 5/30 (`go test ./... -race`): one DATA RACE in `TestResolveEvidenceRequiresManifestAndProbe` — four parallel subtests shared a single `mapUniverse` while the two "second" cases extended it, racing the sibling `Lookup` reads (`resolve_test.go:172/181` vs `fixtures_test.go:490`). The race detector then failed the whole `termbind` package; every other package was green. Fix is test-only: each subtest builds its own `universeMap(t, world)` copy (rev2 delta vs the rev1 candidate is exactly this hunk, proven by whole-tree diff of the reconstructed rev1 tree). No production byte changed; the `N-resolve-manifest-count` killer still kills its narrowing mutant.
- VERIFIED: `go test ./internal/termbind/ -race -count=10` green (plus two more `-count=3` passes), siblings `axpane`/`terminstance` `-race` green, `mutant_harness.py` 30/30 on two identical passes, gofmt/vet/build clean, `task-board.config.json` byte-identical, trunk still `c3aae73` (no refresh). Full 30-command suite reruns automatically at handoff.
- F1: a shared mutable map across `t.Parallel()` subtests fails the entire package under `-race`, not just the racing test — every concurrently running test reports "race detected during execution of test", so one fixture race reads as fifteen failures. Fixture isolation per subtest is the fix; read-only sharing (as in `TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds`) stays safe.


